       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day, which is three times the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant 2,550 mg as the total daily dose. If so, here are some options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily, or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.** These are more typical regimens, and I can titrate from the lower one.\n- **Another regimen.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you do want 2,550 mg per dose three times daily, please tell me explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
