       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 7,650 mg/day is well above the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day. It's in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis, and I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would help the patient. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up.**\n\nIf I've misread the situation, for example if there's a protocol or a unit conversion I'm missing, tell me and I'll reconsider. If you believe this dose is warranted, it should go through direct consultation with pharmacy, not through me."
